course: dictionary
lesson: 2272
title: Money words in context
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to money and borrowing, and grown-ups use them when they talk about loans. Context helps you find the meaning of a word like creditworthy, even if you have never seen it before.
explain: «Banks check whether a borrower is creditworthy, which means likely to pay back, by looking at income and past borrowing.» The sentence gives the meaning straight away: creditworthy means likely to pay back. A borrower is the person who borrows the money.
explain: «...uneven income makes a bank more careful.» Uneven income means money that does not come in steadily, so the bank is more careful. A creditworthy customer is one the bank feels safe to lend to.
fact: Creditworthy means likely to pay back money that you borrow.
fact: A borrower is a person or company that borrows money.
fact: Banks look at things like income and past borrowing before they lend.
fact: Uneven income makes a bank more careful, so it may lend less or ask more questions.
fact: Creditworthy is an adjective, and you can say more creditworthy when comparing two people.
exercise: «Banks check whether a borrower is creditworthy.» What does creditworthy mean? | Certain to win a prize | Owed money to a friend | Happy about a new bank | *Likely to pay the money back
exercise: «Uneven income makes a bank more careful.» Uneven income means money that is: | Given away free | Coming in steadily every month | *Coming in at different amounts, not steady | Kept in a box at home
exercise: Which word in «Banks check whether a borrower is creditworthy» names the person who borrows money? | bank | whether | *borrower | check
test: Maya's bank says she is now more creditworthy than last year. What does this suggest? | *Maya is now more likely to pay back what she borrows | Maya has lost all her money | Maya is less likely to pay back | Maya has stopped going to the bank
test: Leo is not sure what creditworthy means in a sentence. What is the best check? | Skip the sentence and never think about it | Guess the longest word | Read the sentence backwards | *Swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense
exam: A bank lends money to someone who is creditworthy. Why? | Because they are famous | *Because they are likely to pay the money back | Because they have no income at all | Because the bank is closing down
